Third-party components

rustunnel incorporates material from the projects listed below. The original
copyright notices and the licenses under which rustunnel received such
material are set forth below.

The project links against open-source Rust crates, predominantly under the MIT
and/or Apache License 2.0. The authoritative, complete list with exact versions
is in `Cargo.lock` (and the direct dependency declarations in the `Cargo.toml`
files of the `common`, `server` and `client` crates). Notable direct
dependencies include:

  - tokio, tokio-util, futures      (MIT)
  - quinn, quinn-proto              (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  - rustls, tokio-rustls, rcgen     (Apache-2.0 OR MIT / MIT)
  - ring                            (ISC-style; see the crate's LICENSE)
  - clap                            (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  - anyhow                          (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  - tracing, tracing-subscriber     (MIT)
  - serde, toml, bytes, base64      (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  - rand, sha2, aes-gcm, hkdf, md-5 (MIT OR Apache-2.0)

In addition, the frp v2 wire protocol implemented by this project is
interoperable with fatedier/frp (Apache License 2.0). No source code from that
project is contained in this distribution; the compatibility is achieved by
implementing the documented protocol.
